{
  "description": "am-i-crazy: F4 completion-claim guard. Fires on every Stop event and flags completion language (\"tests pass\", \"fixed\", \"verified\", a suspicious pass-count like a claimed count higher than the transcript's actual tool output) that has no matching tool-output evidence earlier in the same turn. This file is opt-in: it ships as hooks.json.example and is inert until you copy it to hooks/hooks.json (see README.md 'The Stop hook'). Once active, an unbacked completion claim exits 2, which Claude Code's Stop event treats as an unconditional block on ending the turn -- this is a hard stop, not a soft annotation.",
  "hooks": {
    "Stop": [
      {
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/scripts/check-completion-claim.sh"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
